    "display_title": "chore: add /cascade, running a spec's steps back to back",
    "event": "pull_request",
    "head_branch": "chore/cascade-skill",
    "head_commit_message": "chore: add /cascade, running a spec's steps back to back\n\nA coordinator session starts every step session itself and waits idle,\nso the depth of sessions started by sessions doesn't grow with the step\ncount. The cascade's state is one issue labelled cascade, edited in place\n(the kit's templates/cascade-issue.md), not prompts layered over comments.\nEach step reports back; a scheduled check catches a stalled step.\n\nAlso: agent-sessions rule 8 in the kit; run-phase notes on long commands,\nprobes, RED-STUB commits and the shotgun check on stacked PRs; the cascade\nlabel in the sync's fixed set.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011AyPi2epF3P2hExj2PS5Uu",
